# Service naming

Do not use these names/suffixes in the service layer:

- `Orchestrator`
- `Helper` / `Util` / `Utils`
- `Manager`
- `Stub` (fake/placeholder in tests, not production)
- `Executor` (collides with `java.util.concurrent`)

`Impl` is allowed only on contracted implementations of a contracted interface
(`ProfileImageServiceImpl`).

Name the class after what it does or the data it owns, not after its caller.
